fixture hazard_loop_stick_held_pit
doc docs/adr/0010, hazards (movement review 4, M1): walking right off the chasm's edge into the spikes, holding right throughout. The respawn is on safe ground 16 u back from the lip (x 453 u, 27 u from the edge) and the stick held through the send-back is ignored until it is let go or turned, so Ash stays put: no second hazard while the stick is still held from the first. (It used to walk Ash straight back off the edge, a respawn-and-fall loop every 29 to 30 frames.)
room test/spike_chasm
spawn 300 384
frames 200
input
  0..199 R
end
expect
  mark die1 0..199 event.hazard=1
  at die1 ground=1 x<=454u
  # What the margin was meant to buy: no second death while the stick is still held from the first.
  never die1+1..die1+60 event.hazard=1
end
